{"title":"Columbus High Invitational","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Columbus High Invitational</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_tournament\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Math tournament\">math tournament</a> run by Columbus High School in Columbus, Georgia, that will occur for the first time on Saturday, February 3, 2007.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Format\">Format</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Columbus_High_Invitational&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Format\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>All competitors are in the same division.  Each school may bring at most two teams of four students each, although indviduals are encouraged to come as well.  The competition will consist of a thirty-five-question individual written test, a relay round modelled on the relay rounds of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=ARML\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"ARML\">ARML</a>, and a countdown round (similar in format to a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MathCounts\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"MathCounts\">MathCounts</a> countdown round) for the top ten students.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Registration\">Registration</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Columbus_High_Invitational&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Registration\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Registration details are available from the information link below.  Registering teams will receive a packet of information on certain competition mathematics topics often not covered in the school curriculum.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Columbus_High_Invitational&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=110469\">Information link</a>, with registration information and invitation letter</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Georgia_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Georgia mathematics competitions\">Georgia mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.gctm.org/math_competitions.htm\">Schedule of Georgia mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017091553\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 12/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4068:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017091553 and revision id 10774. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}